        "original_id": "add83110-3f45-53fc-9bc4-e384a4a435da",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Xawery Żuławski, Brian G. Hutton, Dorota Masłowska\n- Products: Polish-Russian War, Where Eagles Dare, Kelly's Heroes\n- Places: Warsaw\n- Roles: film director, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Brian G. Hutton was born on January 1, 1935, and he was an American actor and film director.\n- Xawery Żuławski was born on December 22, 1971, in Warsaw, and he is a Polish film director.\n- Brian G. Hutton's most notable credits as a film director were the action films \"Where Eagles Dare\" from 1968 and \"Kelly's Heroes\" from 1970.\n- The 2009 Polish film \"Polish-Russian War\" was directed by Xawery Żuławski.\n- The film \"Polish-Russian War\" was based on the novel \"Polish-Russian War under the white-red flag\" by Dorota Masłowska.\n- Brian G. Hutton died on August 19, 2014.",
